#
# Conformance case: foundation/holonic-autonomy-integration
# AC: holonic autonomy/integration duality — Koestler's Janus-faced holon integrity,
# scoped to a declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile (issue #707, C4; per ME9 / #775).
#
# A holon is Janus-faced: it carries a SELF-ASSERTIVE tendency (autonomy, as a whole) and
# an INTEGRATIVE tendency (subordination, as a part). These are CO-EQUAL vantage facets
# (Principle 9) — neither is the primary face. Autonomy/integration is NOT a universal
# well-formedness rule every holon must satisfy; it is a DECLARED logic:HolonicAgencyProfile
# a holarchy adopts (#775). A logic:AgencyAssessment over an (holon, profile) signature
# receives a four-valued logic:agencyVerdict the engine DERIVES. One profile
# (ex:KoestlerProfile, whose logic:selfAssertiveBasis carries ex:CommandCapacity and whose
# logic:integrativeBasis carries ex:SubordinationCapacity) exercises all four verdicts, with
# the structural position of each assessed entity mirroring its agency verdict:
#   * ex:AssessCaptain (holon ex:Captain bears BOTH capacities)
#       → logic:HolonIntegral — the balanced holon: it asserts itself as a whole AND
#       subordinates itself as a part. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict (both
#       co-equal markers hold). Captain is also a structural holon (mid-chain), so C1's
#       logic:isHolon co-fires — a balanced holon is, fittingly, a genuine holon.
#   * ex:AssessPrivate (entity ex:Private bears only ex:SubordinationCapacity)
#       → logic:AutonomyDeficient — the first pathology, a "part" with no autonomy: it
#       integrates but does not assert itself. Reached by negation-as-failure over the
#       self-assertive marker WHILE the integrative marker holds. Private is a structural
#       leaf-part (no proper part of its own), fittingly a part with no autonomy.
#   * ex:AssessWarlord (entity ex:Warlord bears only ex:CommandCapacity)
#       → logic:IntegrationDeficient — the second pathology, a "whole" refusing to
#       integrate: it asserts itself but does not subordinate. The co-equal mirror of the
#       above (NAF over the integrative marker while the self-assertive marker holds).
#       Warlord is a structural root-whole (it has a part but is part of nothing), fittingly
#       a whole refusing to integrate.
#   * ex:AssessInert (entity ex:Inert bears NEITHER capacity)
#       → logic:AgencyUnknown — neither tendency is evidenced, so the integrity question has
#       no positive footing. The first-class fourth value; failure-to-evidence is not
#       integrity. Inert is unattached to the holarchy, fittingly neither asserting nor
#       integrating. (This same verdict would fire for a basis-free profile — no marker
#       could derive — which is why a basis-free profile is unknown, not deficient.)
#
# CO-EQUALITY (Principle 9): logic:selfAssertive and logic:integrative are built by IDENTICAL
# stratum-1 rules, and the two pathology rules are mirror images settling in the same
# stratum, so neither Janus face is privileged. The golden materialized.nq carries both
# markers on ex:AssessCaptain (selfAssertive AND integrative), demonstrating the conjunction.
#
# WELL-FORMEDNESS (the B1 guard): every verdict rule re-binds logic:agencyHolon and
# logic:agencyProfile, so a malformed assessment naming no holon or no profile receives no
# verdict. All four assessments here are well-formed; the malformed-gets-no-verdict guarantee
# is pinned by the Rust unit test holonic_agency_four_valued_verdicts.
#
# DOGFOODING C1 (#704): the assessed entities are wired into a holarchy
# (ex:Private ▷ ex:Captain ▷ ex:Company; ex:Henchman ▷ ex:Warlord), so the C1 holon-kernel
# co-firings (logic:overlaps, logic:isHolon on the mid-chain ex:Captain) are expected on this
# parthood input and are included — suppressing them would misreport the engine. Agency is
# profile-scoped, NOT gated on structural holon-ness, so ex:Inert (unattached) and ex:Private
# (a leaf) still receive verdicts.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so all facts below are duplicated
# there in the named world ex:schema; these are the program axioms.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/holonic-autonomy-integration/> .

# Holarchy: a private nested in a captain nested in a company; a henchman under a warlord.
# Captain is mid-chain (a genuine holon); Warlord is a root-whole; Private/Henchman are leaves.
ex:Private  logic:properPartOf ex:Captain .
ex:Captain  logic:properPartOf ex:Company .
ex:Henchman logic:properPartOf ex:Warlord .

# The declared Koestlerian agency profile: command evidences self-assertion (autonomy),
# subordination evidences integration. The two bases are co-equal (Principle 9).
ex:KoestlerProfile logic:selfAssertiveBasis ex:CommandCapacity ;
    logic:integrativeBasis ex:SubordinationCapacity .

# The capacities each holon bears (the evidence the profile reasons over).
ex:Captain logic:bearsProperty ex:CommandCapacity ;
    logic:bearsProperty ex:SubordinationCapacity .
ex:Private logic:bearsProperty ex:SubordinationCapacity .
ex:Warlord logic:bearsProperty ex:CommandCapacity .
# ex:Inert bears no capacity — neither tendency is evidenced.

# Four agency assessments, all relative to the one declared profile.
ex:AssessCaptain logic:agencyHolon ex:Captain ;
    logic:agencyProfile ex:KoestlerProfile .

ex:AssessPrivate logic:agencyHolon ex:Private ;
    logic:agencyProfile ex:KoestlerProfile .

ex:AssessWarlord logic:agencyHolon ex:Warlord ;
    logic:agencyProfile ex:KoestlerProfile .

ex:AssessInert logic:agencyHolon ex:Inert ;
    logic:agencyProfile ex:KoestlerProfile .
